{"abstract":"This chapter seeks to contribute to discussions of gender-based challenges in women’s esports by adding a regional layer. It explores the phenomenon of women’s esports as manifested in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region of China. The chapter suggests that the framework of the idol (idoru) system—originally Japanese but nowadays largely Asian—helps in understanding the dynamics and branding of Hong Kong women’s esports teams. This perspective invites discussion related to the various commercial interests and powers behind one of the most popular esports teams in Hong Kong, PandaCute.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Jones, Rhys","Wirman, Hanna Elina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798567"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["Hong Kong"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","The Hong Kong Polytechnic University"],"keyword":["China","Digital Games","Esports","Games","Gender","Gender diversity","Hong Kong","Women"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"women s esports in hong kong","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-798567","ids":["itu-eb7938a9-a9a3-4b4d-92e7-91ebf40ce60a"],"keyword":["China","Games","Gender Diversity","Hong Kong","digital games","esports","gender","women"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-AAFAC4E4D4130A7F933562EC507F35F9"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"hk","key":"the hong kong polytechnic university","loc":["Hong Kong","Asia, East"],"name":"The Hong Kong Polytechnic University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU 