{"abstract":"This chapter investigates the official, corpotate response to Overwatch game fandom.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Wirman, Hanna Elina","Jones, Rhys"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381792"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["Hong Kong"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","The Hong Kong Polytechnic University"],"keyword":["Blizzard Entertainment","Co Creativity","Computer games","Digital Games","Fandom","Game design","Games","Overwatch"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"overwatch fandom and the range of corporate responses","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-82767-0","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381792","identifier":[{"id":"85177468342","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-2331ea04-a468-46f1-86dd-4e33b8d52462"],"keyword":["Blizzard Entertainment","Overwatch","co-creativity","computer games","digital games","fandom","game design","games"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-6E824336637EE4E7140A33D4C9C847AC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-82767-0_9","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-82767-0","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Games Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"hk","key":"the hong kong polytechnic university","loc":["Hong Kong","Asia, East"],"name":"The Hong Kong Polytechnic University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanna Elina","key":"wirmanpau","last":"Wirman","locid":"9ba013db-4c4d-41dd-be12-dbe188f67f29","name":"Wirman, Hanna Elina","orcid":"0000-0002-9578-2708","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rhys","key":"jonespau","last":"Jones","name":"Jones, Rhys","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Maria","key":"ruotsalainenpedh","last":"Ruotsalainen","name":"Ruotsalainen, Maria","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Maria","key":"törhönenpedh","last":"Törhönen","name":"Törhönen, Maria","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Veli-Matti","key":"karhulahtipedh","last":"Karhulahti","name":"Karhulahti, Veli-Matti","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-82767-0","eisbn":["9783030827670"],"isbn":["9783030827663"],"pages":"157-177","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Modes of Esports Engagement in Overwatch"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85192603539"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2331ea04-a468-46f1-86dd-4e33b8d52462"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Overwatch Fandom and the Range of Corporate Responses","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381792","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The People’s Republic of China has become the largest digital game soft-ware market in the world. Yet, outside the Chinese game industry itself, very little is known about the local development scene. In this chapter, we approach Chinese regions’ game industry from both a historical and an analytical perspective, particularly by examining how game developers in the PRC, Taiwan, and Hong Kong came to learn game development through copying, imitation, and gradually moving to innovation. The chapter aims at explaining China’s game development history chronologically, starting from the end of the 1980s when Nintendo’s products entered China and pirated products overwhelmed the legally bound regular market until the emergence of indie studios in the 2010s.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nakamura, Akinori","Wirman, Hanna Elina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382941"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["Japan"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ritsumeikan University"],"keyword":["China","Culture","Development","Games","Production"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the development of greater china s games industry from copying to imitation to innovation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5117/9789048551736","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382941","ids":["itu-70768715-7cbf-462d-80f7-28355a652694"],"keyword":["China","Games","Production","culture","development"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8BD360E31AED8486387117E5B792F36C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/47043","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5117/9789048551736","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"jp","key":"ritsumeikan university","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"Ritsumeikan University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Games Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Akinori","key":"nakamurapau","last":"Nakamura","name":"Nakamura, Akinori","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanna Elina","key":"wirmanpau","last":"Wirman","locid":"9ba013db-4c4d-41dd-be12-dbe188f67f29","name":"Wirman, Hanna Elina","orcid":"0000-0002-9578-2708","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Olli","key":"sotamaapedh","last":"Sotamaa","name":"Sotamaa, Olli","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"svelchpedh","last":"Svelch","name":"Svelch, Jan","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5117/9789048551736","pages":"275-292","place":"Amsterdam","publisher":"Amsterdam University Press","status":"p","title":"Game Production Studies"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-70768715-7cbf-462d-80f7-28355a652694"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Development of Greater China’s Games Industry : From Copying to Imitation to Innovation","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382941","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"This essay introduces an ongoing project that aims to enrich the lives of captive orangutans and raise awareness around issues related to their wellbeing and endangerment. Building on experimental and exploratory game design research with orangutans, it addresses a number of examples that highlight the areas of discomfort and uncertainty in human-animal communication and ACI (Animal-Computer Interaction). Cases of unusual play practices and uses of touch screen technology are explored alongside the ethical stance of the research. The essay goes on discussing how play can be used as means to facilitate interaction between individuals of different kind. In play, there is a potential for ‘becoming with’ whom we may first consider a stranger (Haraway 2008). Digital play, in particular, allows a form of mediated communication that eliminates some of the immediate and bodily obstacles and opens up new ways for togetherness in play.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Wirman, Hanna Elina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383067"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Computer games","Design research","Game design","Participation","non human animal play","non human animals"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"spiele für fremde mit fremden orang utans pongo pygmaeus und touchscreen computer games","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.25819/ubsi/9913","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383067","ids":["itu-7a6bcd9a-8e05-45f4-b181-4fef3e6dbea7"],"keyword":["computer games","design research","game design","non-human animal play","non-human animals","participation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-3C1FC52D2DC0FCA25C96B8B5966361F8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.25819/ubsi/9913","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-SA","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86037500/Navigationen_Wirman.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Games Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanna Elina","key":"wirmanpau","last":"Wirman","locid":"9ba013db-4c4d-41dd-be12-dbe188f67f29","name":"Wirman, Hanna Elina","orcid":"0000-0002-9578-2708","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.25819/ubsi/9913","issn":["16191641"],"issue":"1","journal":"Navigationen. Zeitschrift für Medien- und Kulturwissenschaften","pages":"55-72","status":"p","title":"Navigationen. Zeitschrift für Medien- und Kulturwissenschaften","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7a6bcd9a-8e05-45f4-b181-4fef3e6dbea7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Spiele für Fremde/mit Fremden : Orang-Utans (Pongo Pygmaeus) und Touchscreen-Computer-Games","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383067","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"This article discusses researchers’ personal safety by examining a case of studying game arcades in Hong Kong. We approach personal safety from three perspectives as we focus on 1) safety risks associated with specific spaces, 2) risks in meeting and being acquainted with specific people, and 3) risks that are brought along by the theme of a research that may be sensitive. While interview data suggests arcade-goers’ worries over ‘triad’ stereotypes exaggerated by popular culture, police reports and news articles helped us to understand the true and worrying linkages between game arcades and organised crime in Hong Kong even though criminality can by no means be generalised to encompass all arcades.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Wirman, Hanna Elina","Jones, Rhys"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381487"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["Hong Kong"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","The Hong Kong Polytechnic University"],"keyword":["Game Arcades","Hong Kong Research","Organised crime","Personal Safety","Triad Stereotypes"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"invading space on perceived risk and doing research in game arcades","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85752702/I9_GAME_06_WIRMANJONES.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381487","ids":["itu-0ee20f7e-2358-4542-8340-de1cd7ca0c01"],"keyword":["Game Arcades","Hong Kong Research","Organised Crime","Personal Safety","Triad Stereotypes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C58B9E08FAE4CEC4BA150F3333F167A2"],"oa_link":[{"acces