edings of the Digital Games Research Association","publisher":"Digital Games Research Association","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Digital Games Research Association","title_org":"Proceedings of the Digital Games Research Association (DiGRA)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-07d9c64e-23b3-46c4-abf5-5ef73b2e1c9e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Inclusive Game Design for Animals","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381376","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"In the field of human-computer interaction the notion of intuitive use describes the extent to which a human user can subconsciously interact with a product by relying on existing knowledge from similar or identical situations. In animal-computer interaction (ACI) the idea of intuitive use holds great potential as it offers a way to conceptualize and further design better interaction. With the aim to inform future design, this paper discusses how the notion of intuitive use can be applied to interaction design for non-human animal users. We argue that tangible user interfaces together with knowledge transfer from other domains familiar to the animal may allow intuitive use of digital technology. Examples will be drawn from an ongoing game design research project which aims to build digital games for Bornean orangutans.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Wirman, Hanna Elina","Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383744"],"event":{"acronym":"ACE","end":"2015-11-16","place":"Iskandar, Johor, my","start":"2015-11-16","title":"The Second International Congress on Animal Computer Interaction","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["ACI intuitive use digital games interface design tangible user interface orangutan play"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"designing for intuitive use for non human users","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ace2015.info/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/ACE_2015_submission_162.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383744","identifier":[{"id":"84979743372","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-aab2bf7d-b686-4494-9e2c-de38f5cd8bb3"],"keyword":["ACI; intuitive use; digital games; interface design; tangible user interface; orangutan play"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-DB6E11E421878D1DA14C8F0DD0E17009"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ace2015.info/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/ACE_2015_submission_162.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanna Elina","key":"wirmanpau","last":"Wirman","locid":"9ba013db-4c4d-41dd-be12-dbe188f67f29","name":"Wirman, Hanna Elina","orcid":"0000-0002-9578-2708","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"ACE '15: Proceedings of the international conference on Advances in computer entertainment technology"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-aab2bf7d-b686-4494-9e2c-de38f5cd8bb3"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Designing for intuitive use for non-human users","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383744","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
